[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Web3 Wallet Integration: EIP-1193, WalletConnect, Wagmi, and Viem"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Connecting decentralized applications (dApps) to user wallets is a foundational step in Web3 development. Over the years, the tooling has evolved from raw injected providers to highly abstracted, type-safe React hooks. This tutorial explores the modern Web3 stack: EIP-1193 as the baseline standard, WalletConnect for mobile and multi-device pairing, Viem as the modern low-level Ethereum library, and Wagmi as the top-level React wrapper."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. The Foundation: Understanding EIP-1193"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"EIP-1193 is the Ethereum Provider JavaScript API standard. It defines a common interface for Ethereum providers in browser extensions and injected wallets. Instead of relying on proprietary window.ethereum methods directly, dApps interact with a standardized provider interface."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"// Basic EIP-1193 provider request example
async function connectWallet() {
  if (window.ethereum) {
    try {
      const accounts = await window.ethereum.request({ method: 'eth_requestAccounts' });
      console.log('Connected account:', accounts[0]);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('User rejected connection', error);
    }
  } else {
    console.log('Please install MetaMask!');
  }
}"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Bridging Mobile and Desktop with WalletConnect"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"While browser extensions inject window.ethereum effortlessly, mobile wallets and cross-device workflows require a relay infrastructure. WalletConnect establishes a secure, encrypted connection between a dApp and a mobile wallet via a QR code or deep link."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Signaling server relays messages without exposing private keys."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Supports hundreds of mobile wallets out-of-the-box."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Unified session management across multiple device types."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"3. The Modern Low-Level Engine: Viem"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"Viem is a modern, lightweight, and highly performant replacement for older libraries like ethers.js and web3.js. It offers first-class TypeScript support, native ABI encoding/decoding, and direct interaction with EIP-1193 providers."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"import { createWalletClient, custom } from 'viem'
import { mainnet } from 'viem/chains'

const client = createWalletClient({
  chain: mainnet,
  transport: custom(window.ethereum)
})

const [address] = await client.requestAddresses()"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"4. High-Level React State Management: Wagmi"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Built on top of Viem, Wagmi is a collection of React hooks containing everything you need to start working with Ethereum. It manages wallet connection states, automatic refetching, caching, and multi-wallet providers seamlessly."},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"import { useAccount, useConnect, useDisconnect } from 'wagmi'

export function Profile() {
  const { address, isConnected } = useAccount()
  const { connect, connectors } = useConnect()
  const { disconnect } = useDisconnect()

  if (isConnected) {
    return (
      <div>
        <p>Connected to {address}</p>
        <button onClick={() => disconnect()}>Disconnect</button>
      </div>
    )
  }

  return (
    <div>
      {connectors.map((connector) => (
        <button key={connector.id} onClick={() => connect({ connector })}>
          Connect {connector.name}
        </button>
      ))}
    </div>
  )
}"},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"By combining EIP-1193 for standard provider communication, WalletConnect for mobile accessibility, Viem for fast low-level blockchain interaction, and Wagmi for robust React state management, developers can build scalable, type-safe, and user-friendly Web3 applications."}]
